layout: template.njk
slug: change-order-fencing
title: Change order form for fence contractors (free PDF) | Jobchit
description: A free, printable fence change-order form. Record a new fence line, height or material, linear feet, posts and footings, gates, rock hit while digging, old fence removal, the new total and both signatures. No account needed.
heading: Change order for fencing
sub: For a moved fence line, a taller fence, an extra gate or rock hit while digging post holes. Write down the change and get both signatures before the work goes ahead.
tips:
  - Write the old and new fence line in linear feet, and mark any change on a sketch or the site plan.
  - Note the material and style (wood, vinyl, chain link, aluminum or ornamental steel) and the height.
  - For posts, write the spacing, hole depth and whether they get set in concrete.
  - List each gate by width, single or double, and the hardware and latch.
  - If you hit rock, roots or a buried line while digging, write what you found and where, and keep photos.
  - Say who confirmed the property line and the utility locate, and whether HOA approval or a permit changes.
  - Say whether removing and hauling off the old fence is in the price.
  - Both sides sign and date it before the extra work starts. Give the customer a copy.
  - Some states have their own rules for change orders. Check with your state licensing board.
---
